# Track E1 NEG (SCOPE: GuardAccept + genuinely-absent method — the "typo" cell).
#
# A method NAME that is not present on `Guard[T]` NOR on the inner (`int`) must
# REJECT at check-time — never silently accepted and then fabricated at LIR into
# a call to a nonexistent runtime symbol.
#
# Pre-fix (HEAD `482f6f45`): silently accepted, the C backend emitted a call to
# `gorget_guard_nonexistent_zzz` → link error. The exact fabrication class
# (Core #8: known-defect ship).
#
# Post-fix (this track, E1 scope): typechecker reads `DerefWrapperKind::GuardAccept`
# at the terminal fallthrough and emits `E_NoMethodFound`. NOTE: this is an
# INTERIM shape — E2 (deferred) adds the auto-deref path for GuardAccept, at
# which point a name PRESENT on the inner accepts. A name absent on BOTH `Guard`
# and the inner (`int` here — `int` has no `nonexistent_zzz`) still rejects.
void main():
    Mutex[int] m = Mutex[int](42)
    Guard[int] g = m.lock()
    print(g.nonexistent_zzz())
